export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-11-21',
  title: 'Corrected how we describe getting a copy of your data',
  tags: ['accuracy', 'privacy', 'data-deletion'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">November 21, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    Corrected the copy about exporting data so it matches what exists today. Many lists in the app
    (animals, contacts, breeding plans, invoices, and more) can be downloaded from the list itself. For a
    copy of everything, a breeder emails privacy@breederhq.com with the subject "Export my data" and we
    send the records, photos, and documents. There is no self-serve full-account export, and the copy no
    longer implies one or names a specific file format.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Pages updated</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li><a href="/data-deletion" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/data-deletion</a>: the "Exporting Your Data Before Deletion" section now describes the two routes above in place of a JSON and ZIP promise. The "Last Updated" date moved to November 21, 2026. The Quick Options now give the same lead time for an export request as that section: 7 business days.</li>
      <li><a href="/for-breed-clubs" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/for-breed-clubs</a>: the data ownership FAQ answer and the stud book bullet no longer promise a full export at any time, a JSON export, or API access.</li>
      <li><a href="/compare/breederhq-vs-breedercloudpro" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/compare/breederhq-vs-breedercloudpro</a> and <a href="/compare/breederhq-vs-everbreed" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/compare/breederhq-vs-everbreed</a>: the data portability sentence no longer promises a full CSV export at any time; it now says many lists download as CSV and a copy of everything comes on request by email.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</article>
